# Zeitlos -- the LONG demo: about four minutes, for YouTube. Revision 9.
#
# The narration after each "|" is SPOKEN, and spelled for the ear:
# without a speech pack tts's letter-to-sound rules mispronounce common
# words (docs/demo.md, "Spelling for the ear"). Captions are spelled
# normally.
#
#   > run automate /demo/long.zds
#
# Captions are 2x (12x24 pixels a letter), up to two lines. Each
# chapter starts from a clean desktop, so a chapter can be cut, moved or
# dropped by editing only its own block. Language: docs/automate.md.
# Notes: docs/demo.md.
#
# THE RULE: speech and action never overlap. The voice renders at about
# 60% of the CPU, and on hardware anything running beside it -- typing
# included -- made it stutter. So every sentence finishes (narrate and
# say wait) before the next thing happens, and while something happens
# the caption carries the message.
#
# It opens in the synthesised voice and hands over to the recorded one.
# The synthesised voice gets only easy words: it mangles "computer"
# and "FPGA".

reset
interruptible off
caption-size 2
caption-pos bottom
rate 180
type-speed 55
speech on
voice synth
# jfont (Japanese) must already be running: start it before the demo.

# -- 1. what this is ---------------------------------------------------
narrate Hello. I am Zeitlos. | Hello. I am Zeitlos. This is my sin thetic voice.
voice recorded
narrate And this is my recorded voice | And this is my recorded voice: a real person's, joined tuh gheh thur from small pieces of sound.
narrate A computer and an OS, developed together | Zeitlos is a cum pewter, and an operating system, de vel upt tuh gheh thur, so that each can make the other better.
run info at 16 16
narrate One FPGA, 48 MHz, a RISC-V CPU | Every thing you will see runs on one FPGA, at forty eight megahertz, on a risk five processor.
narrate Line drawing, blitter, 8-voice mixer: in hardware | Next to it: a line drawing en jin, a blitter, an eight voice audio mick ser, and USB, all in the same chip.
close info

# -- 2. windows --------------------------------------------------------
narrate Pre-emptive multitasking | Apps run side by side, with pre emptive multi tasking, and a window man ij er built for a one bit screen.
run clock at 420 20
run cal at 60 40
drag 110 45 250 150 900
pause 500
drag 470 26 400 70 700
pause 1200
close cal
close clock

# -- 3. every language -------------------------------------------------
narrate 22 keyboard layouts | Twenty two keyboard layouts, with dead keys and AltGr. The on screen keyboard always shows the one in use.
run text at 16 16
tbicon text font
run keyboard at 150 236
focus text
caption English
type Hello from Zeitlos. It runs at 48 MHz.
key enter
layout de
caption Deutsch
type Grüße aus Bayern! 50 € für Äpfel & Öl.
key enter
layout fr
caption Français
type Bonjour ! Où est le café ? Noël à Genève.
key enter
layout es
caption Español
type ¡Hola! ¿Qué tal? Mañana, señor.
key enter
pause 600
narrate Japanese: romaji becomes kana | Japanese: roe mah jee bee cums kaw nuh as you type.
layout ja-us
type konnichiha. zeitlos desu.
layout us
pause 1200
kill keyboard
kill text

# -- 4. pictures -------------------------------------------------------
# Said first; then the picture is decoded and shown (all at once, when
# view has finished). Tune the pauses to the card: the window must not
# close before the picture is up.
narrate Photos, dithered to one bit | Foe toe graphs, dithered to one bit on the board.
run view /demo/squirrel.pgm at 0 0
key alt+equal
pause 6000
close view
narrate Vector graphics: rendered by Zeitlos | Vector graphics are rendered here, on the fly.
run view /demo/zeitlos.svg at 0 0
key alt+equal
pause 4000
close view

# -- 5. the GPU --------------------------------------------------------
narrate Hardware line drawing | The GPU draws lines in hardware. Grab the cube, and it follows the pointer.
run gpu3d at 220 40
drag 318 146 400 190 900
drag 400 190 300 120 900
key space
key + + +
pause 2000
close gpu3d

# -- 6. drawing --------------------------------------------------------
narrate A MacPaint-inspired paint program | A paint program, in the spih rit of the classics: patterns, shapes and brushes.
run draw at 150 16
origin draw
click 30 50
click 72 256
drag 50 170 320 225 600
click 10 50
click 24 256
drag 120 110 200 168 500
drag 150 132 170 168 300
click 30 30
drag 115 110 160 72 350
drag 160 72 205 110 350
click 10 70
drag 245 18 290 60 400
click 30 10
stroke 90 60 40 75 32 95 40 110 34 125 42
stroke 90 215 40 230 34 245 42 258 38
origin screen
pause 1000
kill draw

# -- 7. music ----------------------------------------------------------
narrate A General MIDI synthesizer | A general middy synthesizer: the cum pewter keyboard is the piano.
run midi /demo/lvb11.mid at 168 100
pause 800
melody 170 e 3 e 3 e m w q n:2 - z c n m:2 - c h m q:2 - c e 3 e 3 e m w q n:3
pause 500
narrate Or play a file | Or play a whole file.
key space
pause 7000
key space
close midi

# -- 8. games ----------------------------------------------------------
narrate A tracker module, and a chess engine playing itself | A tracker module in the background, and a chess en jin playing itself.
run track /audio/retro.mod at 330 20
run chess at 16 16
focus chess
type new demo
key enter
caption A chess engine, playing itself
pause 7000
close chess
# track quits on q, and stops its own mixer channels doing it. NOT
# `close`: its window kills its owner, and a killed track leaves the
# music playing over the next sentence.
focus track
key q
pause 1000
kill track
narrate Games, emulators, and tools to make your own | Games, a chip eight em you later, a see compiler, and a scheme interpreter: tools to make your own.

# -- 9. timeless -------------------------------------------------------
caption White, amber, green or paper
video amber
pause 900
video green
pause 900
video paper
pause 900
video white
narrate Zeitlos -- github.com/machdyne/zeitlos | Zeitlos. Time less cum pewting.
pause 1500
caption-off
reset
end
